From: Lukas Rieger <code@lukasrieger.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wispr: release context when proxy lookup fails

wispr_portal_detect() holds a context reference for the asynchronous
proxy callback. Release it on a NULL proxy result as well as success.
Otherwise each failed PAC lookup leaves the context and its GWeb resolver
alive after the next online check replaces it, retaining DNS sockets until
ConnMan exhausts its descriptor limit.

Clear the completed lookup token before invoking the service callback.
That callback may release the portal owner, so the final unref must not
cancel a proxy lookup whose completion is already being dispatched.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/src/wispr.c
+++ b/src/wispr.c
@@ -1298,17 +1298,19 @@
 	if (!wp_context)
 		return;
 
+	/* The lookup has completed, including when no proxy was found. */
+	wp_context->proxy_token = 0;
+
 	if (!proxy) {
 		wispr_log_proxy_failure(wp_context, "No valid proxy");
 
 		portal_manage_failure_status(wp_context, 0, "no valid proxy");
+		wispr_portal_context_unref(wp_context);
 
 		return;
 	}
 
 	DBG("proxy %s", proxy);
-
-	wp_context->proxy_token = 0;
 
 	proxy_server = parse_proxy(proxy);
 	if (proxy_server) {
